{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1528286-sworn-advice","id":1528286,"title":"SWORN advice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-09T15:58:04-08:00","id":1528286,"title":"SWORN advice","content":"Really sorry if this type of thread has already been created, but wasn't sure how to find it if it has.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm running a HtV2e game set in Appalachia, got 5 players, and asked them to each choose a compact and a conspiracy to be in our world and in the area. They have the option to work with or for them to gain status dots and I can't wait for the players to be forced to choose between two mutually exclusive goals between groups they joined. Should be fun (I know 2nd edition discourages hunters and even cells from being parts of multiple groups, but the conflict they point out is part of the conflict I want to play with lol)<br /> <br /> Compacts: SWORN, The Union, The Recalibrators, Network Zero, Ashwood Abbey<br /> Conspiracies: Cheiron Group, Council of Bones, Task Force Valkyrie, The Lucifuge, Ascending Ones<br /> <br /> Have made a few changes to some to create tensions or fit better, Like Council of Bones is less murdery to being revealed to other hunters. Still huge on the masquerade element though.<br /> <br /> I feel like I know how to make most of these into cool morally ambiguous interactions where the players have to measure the good being done vs the harm being done. Some of the groups are extremely likely to take on an antagonistic role, like Task Force Valkyrie, Cheiron Group, and Ashwood Abbey. And some are more likely to play as largely forces for good, like The Lucifuge, SWORN, The Union, and Ascending Ones.<br /> <br /> I know how to make the more harmful groups tempting, overwhelming resources at the players disposal and strong monsters present. I know how to make most of the largely good groups have tension. Play up the devil and dark urges for the Lucifuge, The Union doesn't want to expend resources outside their home territory, Ascending Ones give diplomatic immunity to a monster for a fragile sense of peace (or sell drugs). <br /> <br /> SWORN however is difficult for me. I don't know what to do to give them tension. I'm not indigenous, and am trying to avoid any stereotypes or using certain monsters out of respect for the cultures and what not, so I will have them largely dealing with cryptids, local vs invasive monsters, looking into disappearances the cops don't want to and such. Trying to tie in how to use their trait in the books of having like traditional knowledge of the areas and the creatures when also using cryptids and such, but I think I can largely thread that needle (although advice would not be dismissed lol)<br /> <br /> My big thing is, how do I make SWORN not just be unabashedly good at an institutional level? Like, yeah, individuals in each of these groups can be good, bad, harmful, helpful, somewhere in between, but I want each of the groups to have tensions that come from being that group. What's a good situation where SWORN can be wrong, can be harmful? I know their TIPI faction is supposed to be sexist, but my players asked me to avoid central conflicts relating to sexism and queerphobia. <br /> <br /> It might help to give an example of a situation I plan to use in the game.<br /> <br /> The player's cell is informed by some of their contacts in the larger hunter society that a SWORN cell near Point Pleasant West Virginia is having trouble with an agitated mothmen population, causing a string of bad luck that could expose the mothmen population and lead to their extinction. When the players start investigating they eventually find out that the Cheiron Group has a nearby lab that created a human-fly like creature that has escaped. This human-fly is what has been causing the agitation in the mothmen population. Where might this scenario be changed (or just a detail added) to add tension to SWORN, or what might be another scenario where they are less than 100% in the right?<br /> <br /> Also wouldn't turn up my nose at situations to make the more antagonistic groups more enticing/good seeming, or the more beneficial groups more tense/harmful-seeming.<br /> <br /> (not interested in arguments about where I placed the groups morally speaking, and I acknowledge that all groups have good and bad actors and good and bad ideologies, hence my question)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25063-diabadass","name":"Diabadass","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T19:24:58-08:00","id":1528293,"title":"","content":"Play up that a &quot;native&quot; monster means the SWORN are more likely to seek a compromise with the monster. Just like the Union isn't willing to go outside its territory, the SWORN will go out of its way to protect a harmful monster if they believe its actually humanity's fault its become harmful<br /> <br /> Basically, SWORN wants to seek a a safe way to live alongside a monster rather than just get rid of it. And if I remember, they are very hostile toward &quot;invasives&quot; which prometheans would def be considered that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-10T10:10:58-08:00","id":1528327,"title":"","content":"Thanks Primordial Newcomer, <br /> <br /> I have two new scenarios I think that they could be involved in; one fully inspired by you and one partially inspired by you and a friend.<br /> <br /> I could have the Ascending Ones have a deal with a promethean (potentially even a golem to tie in culturally). Maybe they are trying to find a like &quot;cure&quot; for the wasteland effect they have. Have to double check the tammuz wasteland effects. They have chosen an isolated part of the Appalachian mountains because its, well, isolated from humans. However some SWORN members have been noticing the Wasteland and are planning to hunt the golem. A difficult middle path solution could be to have the golem complete its current stage of the research and then move, but that would require burning a lot of favors from the Ascending Ones and SWORN.<br /> <br /> The other idea is that a green initiative is helping convert an old coal mining town into building a solar array and managing that. However, to build that solar array, the town has to cut down a significant chunk of a forest. In the forest is a cryptid that SWORN want to protect, partially because they feel if the forest is cut down the cryptid will affect human populations. One SWORN member has put nails into trees, which has lead to loggers deaths. They refuse to turn the member in due to (rightful) distrust of how justice is metered to indigenous people and how many indigenous people go missing or are suicided. The nails combined with the cryptid killing a couple other loggers has attracted the attention of a Union branch who wants to protect their community. Union also knows that the mining company has already pulled out and the vein has run dry. People are too poor to move and no one wants to buy a house in a dying town, so if this transition isn't accomplished, the town is basically dead and the people there will suffer immensely. Do not know a middle path my players could accomplish here, and am happy with that lol. They will have to burn a bridge or two to solve this one (or just let two hunter groups go to war). Might throw in Ashwood Abbey who just wants to hunt the monster for fun, allying with the Union.<br /> <br /> Any other ideas are greatly appreciated! Thanks so much Primordial Newcomer!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25063-diabadass","name":"Diabadass","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}